{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kevinrhaas/chicago/pulls/1041","id":4912610856,"node_id":"PR_kwDOUoK9js8AAAABJNB-KA","html_url":"https://github.com/kevinrhaas/chicago/pull/1041","diff_url":"https://github.com/kevinrhaas/chicago/pull/1041.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/kevinrhaas/chicago/pull/1041.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kevinrhaas/chicago/issues/1041","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kevinrhaas/chicago/pulls/1041/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kevinrhaas/chicago/pulls/1041/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kevinrhaas/chicago/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kevinrhaas/chicago/issues/1041/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kevinrhaas/chicago/statuses/1cbcfb84e3ededd108e96a80b93d3df878eb020f","number":1041,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"T-2793: Add transport studies and named resident authoring","user":{"login":"kevinrhaas","id":4193586,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxOTM1ODY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4193586?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas","html_url":"https://github.com/kevinrhaas","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Adds a development collection for inspecting articulated wagons, an open carriage, a skinned horse, light harness and coupled walk motion. W01 has tapered spokes and chamfered boards; C01 has rounded cushions. The horse has a continuous head/neck boundary, matched headstraps and a selectable grounded diagonal trot. Its scrolling ground preview now follows accumulated distance across clip loops. Existing town placements are retained.\n\nConsolidates resident authoring from PR #1046 using the existing reconstructed 1835 identities Otis Bardwell, Joseph Dufresne and Martin Flynn. Their bodies, workwear, hair and actions are reconstructed without an archival likeness or invented occupation. Licensed source bytes and notices remain pinned. No occupied vehicle, mounted rider or new town resident is enabled.\n\nThe resident build previously stopped at the original raw normal tolerance: run 39192083053 at 9cc7b9ac8 had 21 corners above 0.001. The explicit isolated-CI experiment retains Short2 storage and that tolerance, validates independently probed fan frames, adds source-seam and mesh-invariant checks, and restores original codes on refusal. Defaults and the generic fixture path remain unchanged. Actual pinned Blender acceptance is recorded below; portable tests alone do not qualify the adapter.\n\nIncludes dev ffd4cd34c and its phone memory, picking, confidence overlay, field-log, period-context and fruit-planting updates. The smoke conflict preserves both the upstream black-box notice check and the exact prior-reset record check. The real loss callback now captures its page ID before restore; a caller-level regression covers that return value. Light limits stay unchanged.\n\nValidation at **e1b31c070bfb11d99331aa3d903023cf9865940c**: full preflight PASS: 1,006 checks, zero failed; changelog, ticket-ID and postcommit checks PASS. The supported 58-step liberties-derived tail converged in two laps, with the final lap unchanged. Current horse, harness and carriage regeneration, Khronos validation, sampled sole contact and desktop/mobile study checks are retained with exact input hashes. Installed walk and trot head-fit checks each pass 21 sampled poses; minimum unsigned surface distance is 2.406 mm. These are discrete surface checks, not containment or continuous collision acceptance.\n\nCanonical resident CI: [39196464162](https://github.com/kevinrhaas/chicago/actions/runs/39196464162), pinned to 9e25f2d73, passed the generic fixture and actual local BPy raw-normal/seam guards for all three residents at unchanged 0.001. Maximum raw deltas were 0.0000696794 / 0.0000586337 / 0.0000586337, with zero bad corners or seam groups. All three canonical master/export steps completed. The pipeline FAILED at the next hierarchy-control step: Blender did not add the script directory to Python's search path, causing `ModuleNotFoundError: human_export`. The explicit sibling-path fix plus actual-entrypoint regression (six tests pass) is committed at this head; full preflight PASS1006/0 and postcommit checks PASS. Corrected canonical run [39200379231](https://github.com/kevinrhaas/chicago/actions/runs/39200379231) is preserved on e1b31c070 for the unchanged human authoring diagnostic: generic humans passed, resident job is queued. Hierarchy, hair, Khronos and loaded source/published browser checks did not run; no completed canonical pipeline or photographic acceptance is claimed.\n\nFinal published desktop/mobile coverage: the obsolete18-leg e1b31c070 batch was canceled after confirmed baseline gear penetrations became a merge blocker. All18 reached terminal canceled status; no coverage pass is claimed. A bounded breastcollar/support/pad fit repair is under CPU and visual review before integration, fresh preflight and replacement frozen-head smoke dispatch.\n\nThe older failed canonical and smoke runs remain archived in the tickets repository. All 18 final published stage groups, canonical resident jobs and required PR checks must pass on the frozen commit before merging to dev. Production promotion is outside this PR.\n\nPhotographic human/animal/vehicle quality, period construction review, production LODs, loaded harness/reins, traffic and occupied boarding/riding remain open. Parallel controller, population, tack and motion proposals are saved separately and are not included as completed features. Artifact downloads remain blocked by the unapplied environment network policy; numeric CI logs do not substitute for independent image inspection.\n\n\nBroader fit follow-up: an outside experiment tests corresponding original torso triangles against all 36 unchanged harness meshes over 42 walk/trot poses. Strict edge-plane and barycentric diagnostics confirm actual baseline crossings: 1,386 pairs for a 108-triangle body mask (collar 336, left support 630, right support 420), and 168 left-support pairs for a separate 84-triangle mask. These repeated pose-pair counts are not a count of unique physical defects. This scope was absent from the earlier head and upper-forelimb proofs. Whole-body harness fit is unqualified; T-2801 remains open. An independent baseline strap-routing repair is underway outside the app, alongside local shoulder refinement. The confirmed baseline crossings block this merge until the reviewed gear repair is integrated and validated. The existing source checkpoint and canonical human diagnostic are preserved; no production harness, load, anatomy or riding acceptance is claimed.\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-18T20:37:49Z","updated_at":"2026-10-19T05:41:19Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":null,"assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"kevinrhaas:steward/period-transport-2793","ref":"steward/period-transport-2793","repo":{"id":1384299918,"node_id":"R_kgDOUoK9jg","name":"chicago","full_name":"kevinrhaas/chicago","owner":{"login":"kevinrhaas","id":4193586,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxOTM1ODY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercont